<title>ZAMBIA: Anglovaal to sign Konkola North deal by Feb.</title>
<headline>Anglovaal to sign Konkola North deal by Feb.</headline>
<dateline>LUSAKA 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African mining house Anglovaal is expected to sign an agreement on the development of Zambia Consolidated Copper Mines' (ZCCM) Konkola North mine by February, the Zambia Privatisation Agency (ZPA) said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;An option agreement between Anglovaal and Zambia is expected to be signed within two months,&quot; ZPA chief Valentine Chitalu told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said it was expected that Konkola North was capable of supporting a large scale mining project.</p>
<p>&quot;However, this will only be determined after completing additional drilling and pre-feasibility studies by Avmin,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Avmin is the minerals division of Anglovaal.</p>
</text>
